                             powerful tools we can use. Because                
                             addition is commutative, we can add               
                             terms in any order. This means 3x plus            
                             2y equals 2y plus 3x. The sum stays the           
                             same. We can also group terms using the           
                             associative property with brackets. The           
                             distributive property lets us expand              
                             brackets. If we have five times open              
                             bracket, x plus 3, close bracket, this            
                             equals 5x plus 15. Because we multiply            
                             5 by each term inside the brackets.               
                             Remember, these operations never change           
                             the expressions value. Only its form.             
